{
  "id": "18837_nomikawasu",
  "headword": "{飲|の}み{交|か}わす",
  "reading": "のみかわす",
  "romaji": "nomikawasu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb",
  "gloss": "to drink together; to exchange drinks",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to drink together; to exchange drinks",
      "explanation": "To share drinks with someone, typically alcoholic beverages, in a convivial setting. Implies a mutual, social act of drinking."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "18837_nomikawasu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{酒|さけ}を{飲|の}み{交|か}わす。",
      "english": "We drink sake together.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "18837_nomikawasu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{旧友|きゅうゆう}と{杯|さかずき}を{飲|の}み{交|か}わした。",
      "english": "I shared cups of sake with an old friend.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "18837_nomikawasu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{夜|よる}が{更|ふ}けるまで{仲間|なかま}たちと{飲|の}み{交|か}わしながら、{昔話|むかしばなし}に{花|はな}を{咲|さ}かせた。",
      "english": "We drank together with friends until late at night, chatting happily about old times.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A godan verb ({五段|ごだん}). The {交|か}わす component means to exchange or do mutually, giving the verb its sense of shared, reciprocal drinking. Common objects include {酒|さけ} (sake/alcohol), {杯|さかずき} (sake cup), and ワイン (wine). Often carries a warm, literary tone and appears in descriptions of bonding, reunions, and celebrations.",
